# @req BUG-HIR-SELF-SYMBOL-ID-001
"""
# HIR impl-block lowering keeps the `self` owner symbol scoped

**Category:** Compiler
**Status:** Implemented
**Bug:** doc/08_tracking/bug/hir_flat_ast_impl_lowering_lost_self_symbol_id_2026-08-11.md

## Purpose and Audience

Compiler maintainers working on HIR lowering. When a method body mentions
`self.<field>`, `expressions.spl` resolves that field through
`current_method_self_symbol_id`. Every lowering path that publishes
`current_method_self_type` for an `impl` block must publish the matching
symbol id, and must restore both afterwards, or `self.x` is typed against the
wrong owner (or skipped entirely) for every declaration that follows.

## Scope and Preconditions

The defective path is the flat-AST (`SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP`) impl-block loop in
`module_lowering.spl`. That path is only entered by the self-hosted compiler
during bootstrap; the host binary available to this spec is the Rust seed,
which never runs it. A behavioural repro therefore requires a self-hosted
bootstrap binary and is recorded as blocked in the bug doc. What IS checkable
here, and what actually regressed, is the save/set/restore pairing itself:
commit 83d21f1808 deleted three lines and left the two pieces of `self`
context disagreeing. This spec pins that pairing.

## Primary Workflow

Read the lowering source, locate the impl-block scope, and assert the owner
symbol id is saved, set, and restored alongside the self type.

## Compatibility and Limitations

Source-contract scope only: it proves the scope discipline is present, not the
resulting field types. Pair with a bootstrap run once one is available.
"""

use std.spec.*
use app.io.mod.{file_read_text}

val MODULE_LOWERING = "src/compiler/20.hir/hir_lowering/_Items/module_lowering.spl"

fn lowering_source() -> text:
    return file_read_text(MODULE_LOWERING)

describe "HIR impl-block lowering self-owner scope":
    it "saves the previous owner symbol id before entering an impl block":
        step("Read the flat-AST module lowering source")
        val src = lowering_source()
        step("Confirm the impl scope snapshots the outer owner symbol id")
        expect(src).to_contain("val previous_impl_self_symbol_id = self.current_method_self_symbol_id")

    it "publishes the impl owner as the self symbol for the method loop":
        step("Read the flat-AST module lowering source")
        val src = lowering_source()
        step("Confirm the owner symbol id is set when the owner resolves")
        expect(src).to_contain("self.current_method_self_symbol_id = impl_owner_symbol.id")

    it "restores the outer owner symbol id when the impl block ends":
        step("Read the flat-AST module lowering source")
        val src = lowering_source()
        step("Confirm the saved value is written back so nothing leaks to siblings")
        expect(src).to_contain("self.current_method_self_symbol_id = previous_impl_self_symbol_id")
